{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:15:23Z","created_by_operation":"op_5f029701ca5a4e8ab6cbb19dd506cbec","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_1298c9ef91d5d6a6528a1bc0dba091a7b5c8f7585a7cf7bc864dd19b9e9c3a0a","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"pchalasani/claude-code-tools@ee0f3099c05c snapshot 97d770c6b369880b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_ad5f0258052660f31edb2cfe264ec13d6229f4d418d97330c352dd1a62c1ca12"],"source_ids":["src_dd8ddf3436a95724b46da45b063794b3"],"text":"The >share hook (hooks/share_hook.py) is a standalone stdlib UserPromptSubmit hook that reads session_id/cwd/transcript_path from stdin, writes an fcntl-locked atomic registry, and blocks the prompt to print the handle.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:15:23Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5f029701ca5a4e8ab6cbb19dd506cbec"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:15:23Z","created_by_operation":"op_5f029701ca5a4e8ab6cbb19dd506cbec","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_26415cee010dbd178c9aed47a3f9bdf242cbc1dc0c83f79206572dc9adfd382f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"pchalasani/claude-code-tools@ee0f3099c05c snapshot 97d770c6b369880b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_ce4573cdb7b59defa21e65bd7123570eaebe43acb30608c6334971dfa09a5e48"],"source_ids":["src_dd8ddf3436a95724b46da45b063794b3"],"text":"In a watched channel, '<handle> [question]' opens a Discord thread bound to that session with follow-ups staying in the thread; !list/!handles list active handles; !done/!close/!end tear down the fork immediately.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:15:23Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5f029701ca5a4e8ab6cbb19dd506cbec"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:15:23Z","created_by_operation":"op_5f029701ca5a4e8ab6cbb19dd506cbec","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_27202477a165f912b1e66bb9379a7f51e62d22ab118c365c9e88e760be7c5f7a","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"pchalasani/claude-code-tools@ee0f3099c05c snapshot 97d770c6b369880b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_81c62470128d2740d82250c4e8e336e1df7876e7043731f15131dce8d68eea27"],"source_ids":["src_dd8ddf3436a95724b46da45b063794b3"],"text":"agent-tunnel exposes long-lived local Claude Code sessions ('experts') to teammates over Discord; a session is published at runtime with >share and addressed by a short handle, with each conversation answered against a read-only fork.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:15:23Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5f029701ca5a4e8ab6cbb19dd506cbec"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:15:23Z","created_by_operation":"op_5f029701ca5a4e8ab6cbb19dd506cbec","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_40dfded60246ce70ea24eed84e923f6c75228ab9106bb42aca29977378d07c20","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"pchalasani/claude-code-tools@ee0f3099c05c snapshot 97d770c6b369880b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4191a5db5503dc2b9c3909eada515feb40347d380d37b330f549839a82173825"],"source_ids":["src_dd8ddf3436a95724b46da45b063794b3"],"text":"The spec notes a ToS gray area: consumer plans prohibit making your account available to others, and headless with an API key is described as the unambiguous path.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:15:23Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5f029701ca5a4e8ab6cbb19dd506cbec"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:15:23Z","created_by_operation":"op_5f029701ca5a4e8ab6cbb19dd506cbec","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_53b690b8c997afefeb80c402807cd315948bf5e822d89fdbc86be2c518184484","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"pchalasani/claude-code-tools@ee0f3099c05c snapshot 97d770c6b369880b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_45765a70b31316edb0505c4d22302f750066ff7f0d5813bbc2a2ecc5c3cc3c30"],"source_ids":["src_dd8ddf3436a95724b46da45b063794b3"],"text":"agent-tunnel supports two backends: headless (default) runs claude -p per question with clean JSON I/O, while tmux runs an interactive claude per thread in a private tmux server window, watchable via agent-tunnel watch.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:15:23Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5f029701ca5a4e8ab6cbb19dd506cbec"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:15:23Z","created_by_operation":"op_5f029701ca5a4e8ab6cbb19dd506cbec","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_53eba45573368c50f49eef0606112dcd6cb0b83bffe7d168b1edd34e591bd6e8","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=relevance","setting":"pchalasani/claude-code-tools@ee0f3099c05c snapshot 97d770c6b369880b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_185f42f858c4699d61875df73582ac80d4eaec2348e8861d94e8cab248014085","slc_1c836b7a68d637aefe0dc7c5ab52452f2297c6c5d718b1c007b47c5e25f1e4a7","slc_48355a8fe20f527e999829ecba6b499ad05de19c2caa5c20d43ba1b01987a6f2","slc_4fefd4ee8c5460b2c545edaa1e99d97e1eba8028eea0b7ca425231ea2681972d","slc_f02881ae072062073f9af6ff9fd1a6f47b34ba59dcc1f7592cfcbef03254bce2","slc_f825f30e6e488e26e8d4fca75807ea02b043441d6cc7b3f05483d95cc342aa81"],"source_ids":["src_a8c62bd63bc051fb961a344e24216302"],"text":"The docs include a Zsh shell setup guide covering Oh My Zsh with autosuggestions and syntax-highlighting plugins, the Starship prompt, eza aliases, and Atuin or HSTR history tools.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:15:23Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5f029701ca5a4e8ab6cbb19dd506cbec"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:15:23Z","created_by_operation":"op_5f029701ca5a4e8ab6cbb19dd506cbec","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_56f7787c1dcb25553bcdf1dbe3b58d0caaebd513078f45089da8ab348e1e9fda","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"pchalasani/claude-code-tools@ee0f3099c05c snapshot 97d770c6b369880b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4191a5db5503dc2b9c3909eada515feb40347d380d37b330f549839a82173825"],"source_ids":["src_dd8ddf3436a95724b46da45b063794b3"],"text":"Security model: read-only tools are hard-enforced by the CLI permission layer by default; access is Discord channel membership plus optional user/role allowlists, and the persona's discouragement of leaking secrets is described as a soft layer only.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:15:23Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5f029701ca5a4e8ab6cbb19dd506cbec"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:15:23Z","created_by_operation":"op_5f029701ca5a4e8ab6cbb19dd506cbec","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_672792543a29b3a6dc03c2bac185826b610c4c791a586907f87e34a8ca5eb465","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"pchalasani/claude-code-tools@ee0f3099c05c snapshot 97d770c6b369880b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1c220df1e198c3bbebd671ae2df8bcc712e156d22123aa0c97241601a35c9f21"],"source_ids":["src_dd8ddf3436a95724b46da45b063794b3"],"text":"Write/bash forks save deliverables to .agent-tunnel-out/<thread>/; the bot snapshots and diffs that dir to post new or modified files as Discord attachments, and a wildcard .gitignore keeps deliverables out of git status.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:15:23Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5f029701ca5a4e8ab6cbb19dd506cbec"}
